      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-07-25_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <p>No 1267</p>
        <p>uOUNTY BOROUGH OF %V A KRINGTON.— MUNICIPAL BYE ELECTION 19)3 TO THE ELECTORS OF BT. JOHN'S WARD. LILDIES AND GENTLE%IEN, Owing to the much regretted death of Mr. Coun- cillor Baird a vacancy has arisen in the representa- tion of the Wari on the Town Council, and I have the honour of offering my:elf. in the in erects of the general body of ratepayers and residents, as an indepencheit, c •ndidate for your soffra4es. I Am NOT THE NOMINEE OF ANY PARTY, POLITI- CAL, RELIGIOUS, OR OTHERWISE; RELIEV- ING AS I DO THAT TO SERVE THE BEST INTERESTS OF THE TOWN IS THE TRUE AND PROPER OBJECT TO BE AIMED AT. I WILL NOT BE CONNECTED WITH ANY CLIQUE OR FACTION; EOR WILL I DO THE BIDDING OF ANY BODY OF PEOPLE BUT THE ELECTORS THEMSELVHS. I rlerean,4 a full and searching INQUIRY into the accusations made agaiost several of the members of the Council, in the interests of the accused as well as of the accusers, hut especially in the interests of the ratepayers and the good reputation of our town. I object to all outside interference and dictation, and I trust to the intelligence and good sense of the ratepaye-s to settle our own disputes and manage our own affairs. I am. and always hPve been a Non-Trader and I protested against gentlemen being elected to the Council who had as their °eject to use the position they held as councillors to their own advantage or the adv•intageot their friendr.My views on this matter were well known by the people in general long before severaltoftice-seekers thought of winning a seat by this means after all other means had failed them. I refuse to pledge rryself to any party, political, religious, or otherwise, as I cannot see the advantage of introducing into the discussion of cur local con- cerns any particular set of views which may be held upon Imperial or Parliamentary politica. Neither can I see how the division of the Council into two hostile camps. on a 'question which is largely personal, will benefit the ratepayers, consequently I am not going to waste any time in useless deauncia- Lion of this or that group of c itincillors, but will give my best attention and assistance to all projects which make for the benefit of the whole town and the good of St. Johu'i Ward in particular. If you do me the honour to elect me as one of the representatives of your Ward, it will be my endeavour to see that you get a fair return for the rates you pay, which you do not reeeive at present. Your street paving, lighting, and cewering ere any- thing hut satisfactory, and many of the dwelling- houses in the Ward are amongst the worst in the town, I intend to do all I c:n to have the Cleansing Department's Depot i.ernoved ous of the Ward, as it is in a most unsaitable position at pre- sent. Standing in the midst. of a densely populated neighbourhood, it is a permanent danger to the health of the tuhabitants, and a disgrace to any up-to-date Corporation. I hope to be able to explain to you at my public meeting which will be held during the coning week a simple means of n'opping all unfair, unjust, and dishonest trading with the Corporation, either by members of the Council or their friends, also hope to have he opuortamity of proving to you the unjust means by which the rateable valuation of your buildings is arrived at. thereby causing the working people, and several businesses, to be forced to pay more tan their rightful share of the rates, and at the same time giving other businesses and monopolies an unjust advantage in letting them off without paying anything like their due share of the working expenses of the town. In coulusion Ladies and Gentlemen if I have the honour of securing election for the present vacancy, the term of which is very short viz., 15 months, I will do all in my power to assist you in managing the affairs of our town in the Council to your own advantage and to the advantage of all the ratepayers and to put an end to the disgraceful scenes in the Council Chamber which are a serious injury to the commercial and financial interests of the Borough of Warrington, and are holding us up to the ridicule of all England. By voting for me you will he supporting small whose interests are identical with your own. I am, Ladies and Gent.emen, Yours faithfully, JOHN Bridge street and Ryland, street, Warrington.</p>
