        <p>A SORDID TRAGEDY.</p>
        <p>William Joseph Tuffin, carman,and Mary Stone,house- maid, were sentenced to deathat Surrey Assizes yester- day for the wilful murder of Caroline Tuffin, the male prisoner's wife, at Thames Ditton. After 'Puffin's house had been shut up and the blinds drawn for a fortnight the police broke in; and found Mrs. 'Puffin's dead body on a bed, with shocking injuries to the head, and a chopper by the side. A doctor stated that the woman had been dead a fortnight,during which time the male prisoner had informed the deceased woman's relatives that 'she had died, and had been buried.</p>
        <p>'Tis a short sentence, but one that bears with terrible import. Think what it means to bear a bural; from childhood to youth, from manhood perhaps to grave : the weight of which becomes heavier as It. years roll on. Life stories of such men are fieldoij written; theyare too bitter for words. Our repreSTlA ative, however, recently interviewed a man who borne a load of affliction with true nobility of slori "I came from a family," he said, "that had loog been stricken with kidney disease. Twelve ago I had a severe attack of rheumatic fel'.; It left me in a shattered condition, and 111;1 kidneys, which had never been strong, were weaketi beyond description. My bladder, too, was a source of of trouble. When at my worst I would Ft„t excruciating pains, starting from the small of mY and creeping round with cutting intensity to the oDT.A These pains affected my whole system, and I found ...I"; greatest difficulty in moving about, whilst my breatb!t; was seriously affected. Working as Ido at nightsj tit, constant strain of my kidneys reduced me to a pitokuig plight.' Weary and tired, with ever a constant son back and a difficulty in passing my urine, I longea,gs vain for some relief. I tried various medicines, they were powerless to shift my troubles ; Morse's Indian Root Pills, • however, did 1""'", other so-called remedies failed to do. They cleareu,l4 kidneys and bladder of the glutted matter that had laid in thew, causing me pain, anguish and troub, To-day Mr. W. Ballard, Mayfield Grove, Notting feels perfectly well, and this, he is certain, is Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills. They are apositive for liver and kidney complaints, biliousness,indigest,4oo constipation, piles dyspepsia foul breath, scL",O complexion, and female ailments. They ii;th also a perfect blood purifier, curing ecze,dif pimples, and blotches. Sold by leading chenn and stores, Is.- rjd. per bottle. if unable to 013117,0 where you reside, Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills nlOO, had post free. on receipt of price from The W. H. qg stock Co., Ltd., 21, Farringdon Avenue, London, P•te, It is life stories such as this, of the successful stragt, against adversity, that reconcile us to many of hardships of our-daily lives.</p>
      </div>
